id: pm-rust-o2yr
title: Read canonical pm workspaces without a JavaScript runtime
description: "Ship the first vertical Rust conformance slice: deterministic workspace discovery, strict TOON item decoding, schema-safe core metadata validation, recursive item enumeration, filters, and stable JSON output."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: conformance,query,rust,toon,workspace
created_at: "2026-08-06T21:15:59.978Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-07T00:13:27.161Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-07T00:12:57.642Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-07T00:12:57.642Z"
author: codex
estimated_minutes: 480
acceptance_criteria: A Rust API and binary discover .agents/pm from a workspace or nested path and reject missing trackers deterministically; Real item documents from pm 2026.8.6 decode without Node.js or Bun and preserve unknown extension fields; List output is stable and filters status type and exact id; unit integration property and real-workspace differential tests pass with 100 percent line branch and function coverage
definition_of_ready: Rust 1.90 and pm 2026.8.6 are installed; the canonical companion feature is in progress
value: Makes useful pm context available to low-overhead native agents immediately
impact: Establishes the contract and quality architecture for later mutation and merge slices
outcome: A safe read-only pm-rust CLI and library validated on mature real trackers
why_now: Read paths are non-destructive and expose format incompatibilities before mutation code exists
parent: pm-rust-u4al
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: Delivered the first Rust-native read-only conformance slice and a reproducible cross-platform release gate.
expected_result: A safe read-only Rust SDK and CLI exactly decode canonical pm workspaces with deterministic projections and mandatory green quality gates.
actual_result: "The CLI and SDK match 609 companion items, pass 14 tests at exact 100 percent line/function/region/branch coverage, and use the published pm CLI 2026.8.6 for strict CI health."
notes[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-06T21:15:59.978Z",codex,Uses toon-format 0.5 with default CLI features disabled; dependency behavior is pinned by pm fixture tests
  "2026-08-06T21:54:10.720Z",codex,Real-workspace differential acceptance decoded 609 companion items and exactly matched the official pm 2026.8.6 id status type title priority and parent projection without copying private item contents.
  "2026-08-06T22:27:40.365Z",codex,"CodeRabbit posted nine exact-head findings. Implemented eight: locked Cargo gates,accurate platform wording,optional description decoding,precise conflict markers,fallible newline and flush writes,root-level symlink exclusion,directory-entry error propagation,and root-safe permission tests. Retained the exact empty-array compatibility normalization because toon-format 0.5.0 demonstrably rejects canonical pm field colon space brackets while the official pm 2026.8.6 emits it; all 609 real companion items depend on this boundary and literal array text has a regression test."
  "2026-08-07T00:11:44.058Z",codex,Exact-head CI run 31129047096 proved the git-source npm exec form installed pm-cli without its built binary and failed with pm not found. Replaced it with the published exact @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.8.6 package; the identical strict health command passes locally. This changes only the repository workflow and does not modify pm-cli source.
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-06T21:54:10.720Z",codex,Canonical JavaScript TOON encodes empty arrays as field colon space brackets while toon-format 0.5 expects field bracket zero colon; normalize only that exact complete-line suffix before strict decoding.
files[13]{path,scope,note}:
  .github/dependabot.yml,project,Daily dependency monitoring
  .github/workflows/ci.yml,project,Cross-platform mandatory quality gates
  Cargo.lock,project,Reproducible dependency graph
  Cargo.toml,project,Package and strict lint contract
  CHANGELOG.md,project,pm-changelog generated release record
  src/error.rs,project,Rust-native SDK and CLI implementation
  src/item.rs,project,Rust-native SDK and CLI implementation
  src/lib.rs,project,Rust SDK public surface
  src/main.rs,project,Rust-native SDK and CLI implementation
  src/workspace.rs,project,Rust-native SDK and CLI implementation
  tests/read_contract.rs,project,Filesystem property CLI and failure acceptance suite
  tests/support/main_unit.rs,project,Focused I/O and filesystem error contract tests
  tests/support/workspace_unit.rs,project,Focused I/O and filesystem error contract tests
tests[7]:
  - command: "cargo +nightly llvm-cov --locked --branch --all-targets --all-features --json --output-path /tmp/pm-rust-branch.json && jq -e '.data[0].totals.lines.percent == 100 and .data[0].totals.functions.percent == 100 and .data[0].totals.regions.percent == 100 and .data[0].totals.branches.percent == 100' /tmp/pm-rust-branch.json"
    scope: project
    timeout_seconds: 900
  - command: cargo audit
    scope: project
    timeout_seconds: 600
  - command: cargo clippy --locked --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings
    scope: project
    timeout_seconds: 600
  - command: cargo fmt --all -- --check
    scope: project
    timeout_seconds: 120
  - command: cargo test --locked --all-targets --all-features
    scope: project
    timeout_seconds: 600
  - command: "npx --yes --package=pm-changelog@2026.8.6 -- pm-changelog --pm-root .agents/pm --check --status closed --version Unreleased --conventional --include-links --item-url-base https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/blob/main/.agents/pm --item-ref-style toon --include-metadata"
    scope: project
    timeout_seconds: 300
  - command: pm health --strict-exit
    scope: project
    timeout_seconds: 300
    pm_context_mode: tracker
docs[3]{path,scope,note}:
  docs/COMPATIBILITY.md,project,Exact supported and deliberately unsupported contract
  README.md,project,Public contract and compatibility matrix
  SECURITY.md,project,Security and disclosure policy
close_reason: "Delivered the Rust-native read contract and repaired its CI to invoke the published exact pm CLI 2026.8.6 package; 14 tests plus exact line/function/region/branch coverage, clippy, fmt, RustSec, pm-changelog, and strict pm health pass locally."
body: The first slice intentionally does not mutate canonical workspaces. It validates exact on-disk contracts before transaction and merge work begins.
